 the server afterwards. Nothing was committed.","changes":[{"path":"core/category_api.php","summary":"New category_resolve_handler() that turns a {id}/{name}/null reference into a user id; validation error messages now say 'handler'."},{"path":"core/commands/CategoryAddCommand.php","summary":"Reads `handler` instead of `assigned_to`, resolves and validates it."},{"path":"core/commands/CategoryUpdateCommand.php","summary":"Reads `handler`: missing key keeps the handler, null clears it, an unchanged handler is not validated again."},{"path":"core/commands/CategoryGetCommand.php","summary":"Returns the handler under `handler` instead of `default_handler`."},{"path":"api/soap/mc_project_api.php","summary":"mc_project_rename_category_by_name maps the integer assigned_to to a `handler` payload (0 means null)."},{"path":"manage_proj_cat_update.php","summary":"Sends `handler` ({id} or null) to CategoryUpdateCommand."},{"path":"manage_proj_cat_edit_page.php","summary":"Reads `handler` from the category get result."},{"path":"manage_proj_edit_page.php","summary":"Reads `handler` from the category get result."},{"path":"manage_proj_page.php","summary":"Reads `handler` from the category get result."},{"path":"api/rest/mantisbt_openapi.yaml","summary":"Request schemas use a nullable `handler` object; added Category, CategoryCollection and CategoryResponse schemas and listed them in the Success and Created responses."},{"path":"tests/Mantis/CategoryCommandTest.php","summary":"Existing tests moved to `handler`; new tests for add by id or name, add with no or null handler, update set/keep/clear, not-found codes (and their 404 mapping), and badly formed references."},{"path":"tests/rest/RestProjectCategoryTest.php","summary":"Existing tests moved to `handler`; new tests for 404 by id or name, 400 for an integer handler, set by name, null clear, and handler hidden from anonymous users."},{"path":"tests/soap/CategoryTest.php","summary":"New test: renaming a category with a user id sets the handler and with 0 clears it."}],"acceptance":[{"criterion":"Categories can be created, updated and read with the `handler` field as described (id or name, null clears on update, 404 for a missing user, enabled-user rule, unchanged invalid handler does not block updates, get uses the `handler` key and hides it when there is none or the user has no manage access)","met":true,"evidence":"CategoryCommandTest (testAddWithHandler, testAddWithoutHandler, testUpdateHandler, testHandlerMustExist, testHandlerMustBeUserReference, testAssignedUserMustBeEnabled, testUpdateAllowsUnchangedInvalidHandler) and RestProjectCategoryTest (testProjectCategoryHandlerByNameAndClear, testProjectCategoryHandlerMustExist, testProjectCategoryHandlerHiddenWithoutManageAccess) all pass: `phpunit --filter Category` gives OK (33 tests, 192 assertions)."},{"criterion":"Callers (SOAP, category and project management pages) and the OpenAPI description are updated","met":true,"evidence":"grep finds no `default_handler` and no `'assigned_to' =>` payload left outside lang files. The SOAP test testRenameCategorySetsHandler passes. `redocly lint` reports the file valid; the 3 warnings left were there before."},{"criterion":"The change is covered by tests","met":true,"evidence":"New core, REST and SOAP tests are listed above; existing category tests were moved to the new field."},{"criterion":"The existing test suite still passes","met":true,"evidence":"Full `vendor/bin/phpunit` against a local MySQL 8.0 and PHP server set up like CI: OK (752 tests, 2625 assertions)."}],"human_needed":[{"question":"Should the old `assigned_to` request field still be accepted for a while (marked deprecated), or rejected with an error, instead of being silently ignored?","why":"Clients that still send `assigned_to` now get a success response, but the handler is not set. I followed the issue, which asks to replace the field."},{"question":"Should the SOAP WSDL for mc_project_rename_category_by_name change to take a user reference instead of an integer?","why":"I kept the SOAP contract unchanged (integer, 0 = none) to avoid breaking SOAP clients; only the internal call to the command changed."}],"harness_used":[".github/workflows/mantisbt.yml (CI steps to install MantisBT, start the PHP server and run phpunit)","build/ci_install_mantis.sh and build/ci_post_install.sh (installer call, test project, anonymous user and API token)","Existing config/config_inc.php and tests/bootstrap.php (DB credentials, REST/SOAP host and token)","phpunit.xml and vendor/bin/phpunit","npm script api:validate (redocly lint) for the OpenAPI file","Local Docker image mysql:8.0"],"harness_gaps":[{"file":null,"problem":"No running database or web server, and no script to start them locally. I had to rebuild the CI setup by hand: a MySQL container, the installer call, the post-install SQL, and an API token row that matches the token already in tests/bootstrap.php."},{"file":"build/ci_install_mantis.sh","problem":"It uses `declare -A`, which needs bash 4. It does not run with the default bash 3.2 on macOS, so I called the installer with curl directly."},{"file":null,"problem":"There is no CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md or contributor note for agents about how to run the REST/SOAP test suites locally, or about the API conventions (user reference shape, error code to HTTP status mapping)."},{"file":"api/rest/mantisbt_openapi.yaml","problem":"Before this change, the spec had no schema for category responses, so the response shape was not documented."}]},"ttft_ms":2252,"type":"result","duration_ms":396601,"uuid":"02b42666-4f42-47d4-91c6-b855ca412c78","ttft_stream_ms":1709,"time_to_request_ms":140,"first_content_frame_ms":1709,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":98,"outputTokens":32689,"cacheReadInputTokens":3558879,"cacheCreationInputTokens":98280,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.1521878000000005,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinking